<title>FINLAND: Enso Q1 profit down 28 pct, above fcasts.</title>
<headline>Enso Q1 profit down 28 pct, above fcasts.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to end-March,</p>
<p>					   (million markka unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after financial items		   480 vs 668</p>
<p> Earnings per share (markka)		   1.36 vs 2.06</p>
<p> Net sales					  6,478 vs 6,661</p>
<p> Operating profit				   679 vs 993</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' median forecast for Finnish forest industry group Enso Oy's first-quarter profit after financial items had been 351 million markka (range FIM 258 million to 470 million).  </p>
<p> Depreciation					 440 vs 440</p>
<p> Net financial items		     charge 199 vs 325 charge</p>
<p> Extraordinary items			 gain 450 vs nil</p>
<p> Profit before appropriations, taxes	  930 vs 668</p>
<p> Taxes						   53 vs 14</p>
<p> Minorities				    charge 5 vs 12 charge</p>
<p> Profit before adjustments			872 vs 642</p>
<p> Equity to assets ratio (percent)	    43.6 vs 42.1 end-1996</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Finnish forest industry group is Enso Oy.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358 9 680 50 245</p>
</text>
